      <data key="d27">4.2</data>
      <data key="d21">2</data>
      <data key="d22">471</data>
      <data key="d23">471</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Calculation of fuel consumption and fuel efficiency</data>
      <data key="d24" />
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">False</data>
      <data key="d7">["Subsection"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.1</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">471</data>
      <data key="d23">471</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">Charge-sustaining fuel consumption and fuel efficiency for OVC-HEVs, OVC-FCHVs, NOVC-HEVs and NOVC-FCHVs</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.1.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.1.1</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">471</data>
      <data key="d23">473</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">The charge-sustaining fuel consumption and fuel efficiency for OVC-HEVs and NOVC-HEVs shall be calculated stepwise according to Table A8/6. [TABLE:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.TABLE-A8/6] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.1.EQ-1] [TABLE:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.TABLE-A8/5]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.1.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.1.2</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">473</data>
      <data key="d23">473</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">Charge-sustaining fuel consumption and fuel efficiency for NOVC-FCHVs and OVC-FCHVs</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.1.2.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.1.2.1</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">473</data>
      <data key="d23">476</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">Stepwise procedure for calculating the final test fuel consumption and fuel efficiency results of the charge-sustaining Type 1 test for NOVC-FCHVs and OVC-FCHVs The results shall be calculated in the order described in Table A8/7. All applicable results in the column "Output" shall be recorded. The column "Process" describes the paragraphs to be used for calculation or contains additional calculations. For the purpose of this table, the following nomenclature within the equations and results is used: c complete applicable test cycle; p every applicable cycle phase; for the purpose of EAERcity calculation (as applicable), p shall represent the city driving cycle; CS charge-sustaining [TABLE:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.TABLE-A8/7] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.1.EQ-1] [TABLE:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.TABLE-A8/7] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.1.EQ-2] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.1.EQ-3] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.1.EQ-4] [TABLE:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.TABLE-A8/7]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.1.2.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.1.2.2</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">476</data>
      <data key="d23">476</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">In the case that the correction according to paragraph 1.1.4. of Appendix 2 to this annex was not applied, the following charge-sustaining fuel consumption shall be used: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.2.EQ-1]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.3">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.1.2.3</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.1.2.3</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">476</data>
      <data key="d23">476</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">If the correction of the fuel consumption is required according to paragraph 1.1.3. of Appendix 2 to this annex or in the case that the correction according to paragraph 1.1.4. of Appendix 2 to this annex was applied, the fuel consumption correction coefficient shall be determined according to paragraph 2. of Appendix 2 to this annex. The corrected charge-sustaining fuel consumption shall be determined using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.3.EQ-1] where: is the charge-sustaining fuel consumption of the chargesustaining Type 1 test according to Table A8/7, step No. 2, kg/100 km; is the non-balanced fuel consumption of the charge-sustaining Type 1 test, not corrected for the energy balance, according to Table A8/7, step No. 1, kg/100 km; is the electric energy consumption of the charge-sustaining Type 1 test according to paragraph 4.3. of this annex, Wh/km; is the fuel consumption correction coefficient according to paragraph 2.3.1. of Appendix 2 to this annex, (kg/100 km)/(Wh/km).</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.4">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.1.2.4</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.1.2.4</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">476</data>
      <data key="d23">477</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">This paragraph is applicable to Level 1B and Level 2 only; In the case that phase-specific fuel consumption correction coefficients have not been determined, the phase-specific fuel consumption shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.4.EQ-1] where: is the charge-sustaining fuel consumption of phase p of the charge-sustaining Type 1 test according to Table A8/7, step No. 2, kg/100 km; FC_CS,nb,p is the non-balanced fuel consumption of phase p of the chargesustaining Type 1 test, not corrected for the energy balance, according to Table A8/7, step No. 1, kg/100 km; [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.4.EQ-2] is the electric energy consumption of phase p of the chargesustaining Type 1 test, determined according to paragraph 4.3. of this annex, Wh/km; Kfuel,FCHV is the fuel consumption correction coefficient according to paragraph 2.3.1. of Appendix 2 to this annex, (kg/100 km)/(Wh/km); p is the index of the individual phase within the applicable WLTP test cycle.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.5">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.1.2.5</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.1.2.5</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">477</data>
      <data key="d23">477</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">This paragraph is applicable to Level 1B and Level 2 only; In the case that phase-specific fuel consumption correction coefficients have been determined, the phase-specific fuel consumption shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.1.2.5.EQ-1] where: is the charge-sustaining fuel consumption of phase p of the charge-sustaining Type 1 test according to Table A8/7, step No. 2, kg/100 km; is the non-balanced fuel consumption of phase p of the chargesustaining Type 1 test, not corrected for the energy balance, according to Table A8/7, step No. 1, kg/100 km; EC_DC ,CS,p is the electric energy consumption of phase p of the chargesustaining Type 1 test, determined according to paragraph 4.3. of this annex, Wh/km; K_fuel,FCHV,p is the fuel consumption correction coefficient for the correction of the phase p according to paragraph 2.3.1.2. of Appendix 2 to this annex, (kg/100 km)/(Wh/km); p is the index of the individual phase within the applicable WLTP test cycle.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.2</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">477</data>
      <data key="d23">479</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">The charge-depleting fuel consumption and charge-depleting fuel efficiency for OVC-HEVs and OVC-FCHVs For Level 1A and 4-phase WLTP test in Level 2: The utility factor-weighted charge-depleting fuel consumption FC_CD shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2.EQ-2] is the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex. For OVC-FCHVs, the considered phase j shall be the applicable WLTP test cycle only. In the case that the interpolation method is applied, k shall be the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle of vehicle L n_veh _L. If the transition cycle number driven by vehicle H, n_veh_H, and, if applicable, by an individual vehicle within the vehicle interpolation family, n_veh_ind, is lower than the transition cycle number driven by vehicle L n_veh _L the confirmation cycle of vehicle H and, if applicable, an individual vehicle shall be included in the calculation. The fuel consumption of each phase of the confirmation cycle shall be calculated according to paragraph 6. of Annex B7 with the criteria emission over the complete confirmation cycle and the applicable CO2 phase value [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2.EQ-3] which shall be corrected to an electric energy consumption of zero, EC_DC,CD,j = 0 , by using the CO2 mass correction coefficient (K_CO2) according to Appendix 2 to this annex. For Level 1B and 3-phase WLTP test in Level 2 The charge-depleting fuel efficiency FE_CD shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2.EQ-4] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2.EQ-5] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2.EQ-6] where: is the charge-depleting fuel efficiency, km/l; in the case of OVC- HEVs and kg/km in the case of OVC-FCHVs; actual charge-depleting range defined in paragraph 4.4.5. of this annex, km; in the case of OVC-HEVs and in paragraph 4.4.7. of this annex in the case of OVC-FCHVs, km; is the fuel efficiency for cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, determined according to paragraph 6. of Annex B7, km/l; in the case of OVC-HEVs and kg/km in the case of OVC- FCHVs; [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2.EQ-7] ; is the index number for the considered cycle; n is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven up to the end of the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex d_c is the distance driven in the applicable WLTP test cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; d_n is the distance driven in the applicable WLTP test cycle n of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; k_CD For OVC-HEVs [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2.EQ-8] For OVC-FCHVs [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.2.EQ-9] FECS,declared is the charge-sustaining fuel efficiency declaration according to Table A8/7 Step5, km/kg; FE_CD ,n is the fuel efficiency of the applicable WLTP test cycle n of the chargedepleting Type 1 test, km/kg; FE_CD ,avg,n−1 is the arithmetic average fuel efficiency of the charge-depleting Type 1 test from the beginning up to and including the applicable WLTP test cycle (n- 1), km/kg.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.3">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.2.3</data>
      <data key="d27">4.2.3</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">479</data>
      <data key="d23">480</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">This paragraph is applicable only for Level 1A and 4-phase WLTP test in Level 2 Utility factor-weighted fuel consumption for OVC-HEVs and OVC-FCHVs The utility factor-weighted fuel consumption for OVC-HEVs from the chargedepleting and charge-sustaining Type 1 test shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.3.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.3.EQ-2] The utility factor-weighted fuel consumption for OVC-FCHVs from the charge-depleting and charge-sustaining Type 1 test shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.3.EQ-3] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.3.EQ-4] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.3.EQ-5] where: is the utility factor-weighted fuel consumption, kg/100km; is the utility factor of phase j according to Appendix 5 to this annex; [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.3.EQ-6] is the fuel consumption of phase j of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, determined according to paragraph 6. of Annex B7, kg/100km; FC_CD ,declared is the declared charge-depleting fuel consumption according to Table A8/9a, step no. 11, kg/100km; FC_CD ,ave is the arithmetic average charge-depleting CO2 emission according to Table A8/9a, step no. 10, kg/100km; FC_CS is the fuel consumption determined according to Table A8/7, step No. 5, kg/100km; j is the index number for the considered phase; k is the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex. For OVC-FCHVs, the considered phase j shall be the applicable WLTP test cycle only. In the case that the interpolation method is applied, k shall be the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle of vehicle L n_veh _L. If the transition cycle number driven by vehicle H, n_veh_H, and, if applicable, by an individual vehicle within the vehicle interpolation family n_veh_ind is lower than the transition cycle number driven by vehicle L, n_veh_L , the confirmation cycle of vehicle H and, if applicable, an individual vehicle shall be included in the calculation. The fuel consumption of each phase of the confirmation cycle shall be calculated according to paragraph 6. of Annex B7 with the criteria emission over the complete confirmation cycle and the applicable CO2 phase value which shall be corrected to an electric energy consumption of [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.2.3.EQ-7] zero EC_DC,CD,j = 0 by using the CO2 mass correction coefficient (KCO2) according to Appendix 2 to this annex.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3</data>
      <data key="d21">2</data>
      <data key="d22">480</data>
      <data key="d23">481</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Calculation of electric energy consumption</data>
      <data key="d24">For the determination of the electric energy consumption based on the current and voltage determined according to Appendix 3 to this annex, the following equations shall be used: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.EQ-1] where: is the electric energy consumption over the considered period j based on the REESS depletion, Wh/km; is the electric energy change of all REESSs during the considered period j, Wh; is the distance driven in the considered period j, km; and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.EQ-2] where: is the electric energy change of REESS i during the considered period j, Wh; and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.EQ-3] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.EQ-4] is the time at the beginning of the considered period j, s; is the time at the end of the considered period j, s; is the electric current of REESS i during the considered period j determined according to Appendix 3 to this annex, A; is the index number of the considered REESS; is the total number of REESS; is the index for the considered period, where a period can be any combination of phases or cycles; is the conversion factor from Ws to Wh.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Subsection", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.1</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">481</data>
      <data key="d23">482</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">This paragraph is applicable only for Level 1A and 4-phase WLTP test in Level 2 Utility factor-weighted charge-depleting electric energy consumption based on the recharged electric energy from the mains for OVC-HEVs and OVC- FCHVs The utility factor-weighted charge-depleting electric energy consumption based on the recharged electric energy from the mains shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.1.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.1.EQ-2] where: is the electric energy consumption based on the REESS depletion of phase j of the charge-depleting Type 1 test according to paragraph 4.3. of this annex, Wh/km; [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.1.EQ-3] is the recharged electric energy from the mains determined according to paragraph 3.2.4.6. of this annex, Wh; is the electric energy change of all REESSs of phase j according to paragraph 4.3. of this annex, Wh; is the index number for the considered phase; [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.1.EQ-4] is the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex. In the case that the interpolation method is applied, k is the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle of L,n_veh_L. For OVC-FCHVs, the considered phase j shall be the applicable WLTP test cycle only.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.2</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">482</data>
      <data key="d23">482</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">This paragraph is applicable only for Level 1A and results after 4 phases in Level 2 Utility factor-weighted electric energy consumption based on the recharged electric energy from the mains for OVC-HEVs and OVC-FCHVs The utility factor-weighted electric energy consumption based on the recharged electric energy from the mains shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.2.EQ-1] where: is the utility factor-weighted electric energy consumption based on the recharged electric energy from the mains, Wh/km; is the utility factor of phase j according to Appendix 5 to this annex; is the declared charge-depleting electric energy consumption based on the recharged electric energy from the mains for OVC-HEVs according to Table A8/8, step 14 and for OVC-FCHVs according to Table A8/9a, step 11, Wh/km; j is the index number for the considered phase; k is the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex. In the case that the interpolation method is applied, k is the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle of vehicle L, nveh_L. For OVC-FCHVs, the considered phase j shall be the applicable WLTP test cycle only.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.3">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.3</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.3</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">482</data>
      <data key="d23">482</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Electric energy consumption for OVC-HEVs and OVC-FCHVs (as applicable)</data>
      <data key="d24" />
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">False</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.3.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.3</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.3.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.3.1</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">482</data>
      <data key="d23">483</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Determination of cycle-specific electric energy consumption</data>
      <data key="d24">The electric energy consumption based on the recharged electric energy from the mains and the equivalent all-electric range shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.3.1.EQ-1] where: EC is the electric energy consumption of the applicable WLTP test cycle based on the recharged electric energy from the mains and the equivalent all-electric range, Wh/km; EAC is the recharged electric energy from the mains according to paragraph 3.2.4.6. of this annex, Wh; EAER is the equivalent all-electric range for OVC-HEVs according to paragraph 4.4.4.1. of this annex and for OVC-FCHVs according to paragraph 4.4.6.1. of this annex, km.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.3.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.3</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.3.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.3.2</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">483</data>
      <data key="d23">483</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Determination of phase-specific electric energy consumption</data>
      <data key="d24">The phase-specific electric energy consumption based on the recharged electric energy from the mains and the phase-specific equivalent all-electric range shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.3.2.EQ-1]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.4</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.4</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">483</data>
      <data key="d23">483</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Electric energy consumption of PEVs</data>
      <data key="d24" />
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">False</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.4.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.4.1</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">483</data>
      <data key="d23">483</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">The electric energy consumption determined in this paragraph shall be calculated only if the vehicle was able to follow the applicable WLTP test cycle within the speed trace tolerances according to paragraph 2.6.8.3.1.2. of Annex B6 during the entire considered period.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.4.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.4.2</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">483</data>
      <data key="d23">483</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Electric energy consumption determination of the applicable WLTP test cycle</data>
      <data key="d24">The electric energy consumption of the applicable WLTP test cycle based on the recharged electric energy from the mains and the pure electric range shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4.2.EQ-1]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4.3">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.4.3</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.4.3</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">483</data>
      <data key="d23">484</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">This paragraph is applicable to Level 1A and Level 2 only; Electric energy consumption determination of the applicable WLTP city test cycle (if applicable) The electric energy consumption of the applicable WLTP city test cycle based on the recharged electric energy from the mains and the pure electric range for the applicable WLTP city test cycle shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4.3.EQ-1]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4.4">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.3.4.4</data>
      <data key="d27">4.3.4.4</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">484</data>
      <data key="d23">484</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Electric energy consumption determination of the phase-specific values</data>
      <data key="d24">The electric energy consumption of each individual phase based on the recharged electric energy from the mains and the phase-specific pure electric range shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.3.4.4.EQ-1]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4</data>
      <data key="d21">2</data>
      <data key="d22">484</data>
      <data key="d23">484</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Calculation of electric ranges</data>
      <data key="d24" />
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">False</data>
      <data key="d7">["Subsection"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.1</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">484</data>
      <data key="d23">484</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">All-electric ranges AER and AER_city for OVC-HEVs and OVC-FCHVs (as</data>
      <data key="d24">applicable)</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.1.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.1.1</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">484</data>
      <data key="d23">484</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">All-electric range AER</data>
      <data key="d24">The all-electric range AER for OVC-HEVs shall be determined from the charge-depleting Type 1 test described in paragraph 3.2.4.3. of this annex as part of the Option 1 test sequence and referenced in paragraph 3.2.6.1. of this annex as part of the Option 3 test sequence by driving the applicable WLTP test cycle according to paragraph 1.4.2.1. of this annex. The AER is defined as the distance driven from the beginning of the charge-depleting Type 1 test to the point in time where the combustion engine or fuel cell in the case of OVC- FCHVs starts consuming fuel.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.1.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.1.2</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">484</data>
      <data key="d23">484</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">All-electric range city AER_city</data>
      <data key="d24">This paragraph is applicable to Level 1A and Level 2 only;</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.1.2.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.1.2.1</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">484</data>
      <data key="d23">485</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">The all-electric range city AER_city for OVC-HEVs or OVC-FCHVs shall be</data>
      <data key="d24">determined from the charge-depleting Type 1 test described in paragraphs 3.2.4.1., 3.2.4.2. and 3.2.4.3. of this annex as part of the Option 1 test sequence by driving the applicable WLTP city test cycle according to paragraph 1.4.2.2. of this annex. The AER_city is defined as the distance driven from the beginning of the charge-depleting Type 1 test to the point in time where the combustion engine or fuel cell in the case of OVC-FCHVs starts consuming fuel. The point in time where the combustion engine or fuel cell in the case of OVC- FCHVs starts consuming fuel shall be considered as the break-off criterion and shall replace the break-off criterion described in paragraph 3.2.4.4.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.1.2.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.1.2.2</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">485</data>
      <data key="d23">486</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">As an alternative to paragraph 4.4.1.2.1. of this annex, the all-electric range city AER_city may be determined from the charge-depleting Type 1 test described in paragraph 3.2.4.3. of this annex by driving the applicable WLTP test cycles according to paragraph 1.4.2.1. of this annex. In that case, the charge-depleting Type 1 test by driving the applicable WLTP city test cycle shall be omitted and the all-electric range city AER_city shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2.2.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2.2.EQ-2] where: is the electric energy change of all REESSs during phase j, Wh; is the index number of the considered phase; k+1 is the number of the phases driven from the beginning of the test until the point in time when the combustion engine starts consuming fuel; and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2.2.EQ-3] where: is the electric energy consumption for the j^th pure electrically driven WLTP city test cycle of the charge-depleting Type 1 test according to paragraph 3.2.4.3. of this annex by driving applicable WLTP test cycles, Wh/km; Kcity,j is the weighting factor for the j^th pure electrically driven applicable WLTP city test cycle of the charge-depleting Type 1 test according to paragraph 3.2.4.3. of this annex by driving applicable WLTP test cycles; [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2.2.EQ-4] is the index number of the pure electrically driven applicable WLTP city test cycle considered; is the number of pure electrically driven applicable WLTP city test cycles; and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2.2.EQ-5] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.1.2.2.EQ-6]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.2</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">486</data>
      <data key="d23">486</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Pure electric range for PEVs</data>
      <data key="d24">The ranges determined in this paragraph shall only be calculated if the vehicle was able to follow the applicable WLTP test cycle within the speed trace tolerances according to paragraph 2.6.8.3.1.2. of Annex B6 during the entire considered period.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.2.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.2.1</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">486</data>
      <data key="d23">486</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">Determination of the pure electric ranges when the shortened Type 1 test procedure is applied</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.2.1.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.2.1.1</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">486</data>
      <data key="d23">487</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">The pure electric range for the applicable WLTP test cycle PERWLTC for PEVs shall be calculated from the shortened Type 1 test as described in paragraph 3.4.4.2. of this annex using the following equations: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.1.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.1.EQ-2] and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.1.EQ-3] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.1.EQ-4] where: is the weighting factor for the applicable WLTP test cycle of DS_j of the shortened Type 1 test procedure; ∆E_REESS ,WLTC ,1 is the electric energy change of all REESSs during the applicable WLTP test cycle of DS1 of the shortened Type 1 test procedure, Wh.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.2.1.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.2.1.2</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">487</data>
      <data key="d23">488</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Pure Electric Range city (PER_city) (if applicable)</data>
      <data key="d24">This paragraph is applicable to Level 1A and Level 2 only; The pure electric range for the applicable WLTP city test cycle PER city for PEVs shall be calculated from the shortened Type 1 test procedure as described in paragraph 3.4.4.2. of this annex using the following equations: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.2.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.2.EQ-2] where: is the electric energy consumption for the applicable WLTP city test cycle where the first applicable WLTP city test cycle of DS1 is indicated as j = 1, the second applicable WLTP city test cycle of DS1 is indicated as j = 2, the first applicable WLTP city test cycle of DS2 is indicated as j = 3 and the second applicable WLTP city test cycle of DS2 is indicated as j = 4 of the shortened Type 1 test procedure according to paragraph 4.3. of this annex, Wh/km; Kcity,j is the weighting factor for the applicable WLTP city test cycle where the first applicable WLTP city test cycle of DS1 is indicated as j = 1, the second applicable WLTP city test cycle of DS1 is indicated as j = 2, the first applicable WLTP city test cycle of DS2 is indicated as j = 3 and the second applicable WLTP city test cycle of DS2 is indicated as j = 4, and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.2.EQ-3] where: is the energy change of all REESSs during the first applicable WLTP city test cycle of DS1 of the shortened Type 1 test procedure, Wh.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.3">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.2.1.3</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.2.1.3</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">488</data>
      <data key="d23">489</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">The phase-specific pure electric range PERp for PEVs shall be calculated from the Type 1 test as described in paragraph 3.4.4.2. of this annex by using the following equations: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.3.EQ-1] In the case that phase p = low and phase p = medium, the following equations shall be used: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.3.EQ-2] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.3.EQ-3] where: is the energy change of all REESSs during the first phase p of DS1 of the shortened Type 1 test procedure, Wh. In the case that phase p = high and phase p = extra high, the following equations shall be used: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.3.EQ-4] where: EC_DC ,p,j is the electric energy consumption for phase p of DSj of the shortened Type 1 test procedure according to paragraph 4.3. of this annex, Wh/km; K_p,j is the weighting factor for phase p of DS_j of the shortened Type 1 test procedure and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.1.3.EQ-5] where: is the electric energy change of all REESSs during the first phase p of DS1 of the shortened Type 1 test procedure, Wh.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.2.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.2.2</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">489</data>
      <data key="d23">489</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">Determination of the pure electric ranges when the consecutive cycle Type 1 test procedure is applied</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.2.2.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.2.2.1</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">489</data>
      <data key="d23">490</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">The pure electric range for the applicable WLTP test cycle PER_WLTP for PEVs shall be calculated from the Type 1 test as described in paragraph 3.4.4.1. of this annex using the following equations: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.1.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.1.EQ-2] where: is the electric energy change of all REESSs during phase j of the consecutive cycle Type 1 test procedure, Wh; is the index number of the phase; is the number of phases driven from the beginning up to and including the phase where the break-off criterion is reached; and: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.1.EQ-3] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.1.EQ-4] is the whole number of complete applicable WLTP test cycles driven; and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.1.EQ-5] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.1.EQ-6] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.1.EQ-7] where: is the electric energy change of all REESSs during the first applicable WLTP test cycle of the consecutive cycle Type 1 test procedure, Wh.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.2.2.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.2.2.2</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">490</data>
      <data key="d23">490</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Pure Electric Range city (PERcity) (if applicable)</data>
      <data key="d24">This paragraph is applicable to Level 1A and Level 2 only; The pure electric range for the WLTP city test cycle PERcity for PEVs shall be calculated from the Type 1 test as described in paragraph 3.4.4.1. of this annex using the following equations: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.2.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.2.EQ-2] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.2.EQ-3] where: is the electric energy change of all REESSs during the first applicable WLTP city test cycle of the consecutive cycle Type 1 test procedure, Wh.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.3">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.2.2.3</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.2.2.3</data>
      <data key="d21">5</data>
      <data key="d22">490</data>
      <data key="d23">491</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">The phase-specific pure electric range PERp for PEVs shall be calculated from the Type 1 test as described in paragraph 3.4.4.1. of this annex using the following equations: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.3.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.3.EQ-2] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.2.2.3.EQ-3]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.3">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.3</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.3</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">491</data>
      <data key="d23">491</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Charge-depleting cycle range for OVC-HEVs and OVC-FCHVs</data>
      <data key="d24">The charge-depleting cycle range RCDC shall be determined from the chargedepleting Type 1 test described in paragraph 3.2.4.3. of this annex as part of the Option 1 test sequence and referenced in paragraph 3.2.6.1. of this annex as part of the Option 3 test sequence. The R_CDC is the distance driven from the beginning of the charge-depleting Type 1 test to the end of the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.4</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.4</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">491</data>
      <data key="d23">491</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Equivalent all-electric range for OVC-HEVs</data>
      <data key="d24" />
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">False</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.4.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.4.1</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">491</data>
      <data key="d23">492</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Determination of cycle-specific equivalent all-electric range</data>
      <data key="d24">The cycle-specific equivalent all-electric range shall be calculated using the following equation: For Level 1A and 4-phase WLTP test in Level 2; [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.1.EQ-1] For Level 1B and 3-phase WLTP test in Level 2; where: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.1.EQ-2] is the cycle-specific equivalent all-electric range, km; is the arithmetic average of charge-sustaining CO2 emission according to Table A8/5, step No. 6 (MCO2,CS,c,6) for Level 1A and 4-phase WLTP test in Level 2, g/km; MCO2,CS,declared is the declared charge-sustaining CO2 emission according to Table A8/5, step No. 6 (MCO2,CS,c,declared) for Level 1B and 3-phase WLTP test in Level 2, g/km; MCO2,CD,avg,ave is the arithmetic average of M_CO2,CD,avg calculated for all individual charge-depleting tests according to the equation below, g/km; R_CDC is the charge-depleting cycle range according to paragraph 4.4.3. of this annex, km; RCDC,ave is the arithmetic average of charge-depleting cycle range (R_CDC) calculated for all individual charge-depleting tests, km; and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.1.EQ-3]</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.4.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.4.2</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">492</data>
      <data key="d23">494</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Determination of the phase-specific equivalent all-electric range</data>
      <data key="d24">The phase-specific equivalent all-electric range shall be calculated using the following equation: For Level 1A and 4-phase WLTP test in Level 2: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.2.EQ-1] For Level 1B and 3-phase WLTP test in Level 2: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.2.EQ-2] is the phase-specific CO2 emission from the chargesustaining Type 1 test for the considered phase p according to Table A8/5, step No. 6 (MCO2,CS,p,6), g/km; is the arithmetic average of M_CO2,CD,avg,p calculated for all individual charge-depleting tests according to the equation below, g/km; are the electric energy changes of all REESSs during the considered phase j, Wh; is the arithmetic average of electric energy changes of all REESSs (∆E_REESS,j) during the considered phase j calculated for all individual charge-depleting tests, Wh ; ECDC,CD,p,ave is the arithmetic average of electric energy consumption over the considered phase p ( EC_DC,CD,p) calculated according to the equation below for all individual chargedepleting tests, Wh/km; j is the index number of the considered phase; k is the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle n according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex; and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.2.EQ-3] where: is the charge-depleting CO2 emission for the considered phase p, g/km; is the CO2 emission determined according to paragraph 3.2.1. of Annex B7 of phase p in cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, g/km; is the distance driven in the considered phase p of cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; is the index number of the considered applicable WLTP test cycle; is the index of the individual phase within the applicable WLTP test cycle; is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven up to the end of the transition cycle n according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex; and: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.2.EQ-4] where: is the electric energy consumption of the considered phase p based on the REESS depletion of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, Wh/km; is the electric energy consumption of the considered phase p of cycle c based on the REESS depletion of the charge-depleting Type 1 test according to paragraph 4.3. of this annex, Wh/km; [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.4.2.EQ-5] is the distance driven in the considered phase p of cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; is the index number of the considered applicable WLTP test cycle; is the index of the individual phase within the applicable WLTP test cycle; is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven up to the end of the transition cycle n according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex. For Level 1A and 4-phase WLTP test in Level 2: The considered phase shall be the low phase, medium phase, high phase, extra high phase, and the city driving cycle. For Level 1B and 3-phase WLTP test in Level 2: The considered phase shall be the low phase, medium phase and high phase.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.5">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.5</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.5</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">494</data>
      <data key="d23">495</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Actual charge-depleting range for OVC-HEVs</data>
      <data key="d24">The actual charge-depleting range shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.5.EQ-1] where: is the actual charge-depleting range, km; is the charge-sustaining CO2 emission according to Table A8/5, step No. 7, g/km; is the CO2 emission of the applicable WLTP test cycle n of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, g/km; M_CO2,CD,avg,n−1 is the CO2 emission of the charge-depleting Type 1 test from the beginning of the charge-depleting Type 1 test up to and including the applicable WLTP test cycle (n-1), g/km; d_c is the distance driven in the applicable WLTP test cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; d_n is the distance driven in the applicable WLTP test cycle n of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; c is the index number of the considered applicable WLTP test cycle; n is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven including the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex; and: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.5.EQ-2] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.5.EQ-3] is the distance driven in the applicable WLTP test cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; is the index number of the considered applicable WLTP test cycle; is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven including the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.6</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.6</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">495</data>
      <data key="d23">495</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Equivalent all-electric range for OVC-FCHVs</data>
      <data key="d24" />
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">False</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.1">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.6.1</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.6.1</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">495</data>
      <data key="d23">496</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Determination of cycle-specific equivalent all-electric range</data>
      <data key="d24">The cycle-specific equivalent all-electric range shall be calculated using the following equation: For Level 1A and 4-phase WLTP test in Level 2 [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.1.EQ-1] [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.1.EQ-2] For Level 1B and 3-phase WLTP test in Level 2 where: is the cycle-specific equivalent all-electric range, km; is the charge-sustaining fuel consumption according to Table A8/7 Step 4, kg/100km; FC_CD,avg,ave is the arithmetic average of the charge-depleting fuel consumption FC_CD,avg calculated for all individual chargedepleting tests according to the equation below, kg/100km; FECS,declared is the charge-sustaining fuel efficiency declaration according to [TABLE:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.TABLE-A8/7] RCDC,ave is the arithmetic average of charge-depleting cycle range (R_CDC) calculated for all individual charge-depleting tests according to paragraph 4.4.3. of this annex, km; R_CDC is the charge-depleting cycle range (R_CDC) according to paragraph 4.4.3 of this annex, km; and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.1.EQ-3] and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.1.EQ-4] The considered phase j shall be the applicable WLTP test cycle only.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.6.2</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.6.2</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">496</data>
      <data key="d23">497</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8" />
      <data key="d24">Determination of the phase-specific equivalent all-electric range for OVC- FCHV The phase-specific equivalent all-electric range shall be calculated using the following equation: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.2.EQ-1] where: is the phase-specific equivalent all-electric range for the considered phase p, km; is the phase-specific fuel consumption from the chargesustaining Type 1 test for the considered phase p according to Table A8/7, step No. 4, kg/100km; is the arithmetic average of FC_CD,avg,p calculated for all individual charge-depleting tests according to the equation below, kg/100km; ∆EREESS ,j,ave is the arithmetic average of the electric energy changes of all REESSs (∆E_REESS,j) during the considered phase j calculated for all individual charge-depleting tests, Wh; ECDC,CD,p,ave is the arithmetic average of electric energy consumption over the considered phase p ( EC_DC,CD,p) calculated according to the equation below for all individual chargedepleting tests, Wh/km; j is the index number of the considered phase; k is the number of phases driven up to the end of the transition cycle n according to paragraph 3.2.4.4 of this annex; and [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.2.EQ-2] where: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.2.EQ-3] is the charge-depleting fuel consumption for the considered phase p, kg/100km; is the fuel consumption determined according to paragraph 3.2.1. of Annex B7 of phase p in cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, kg/100km; is the distance driven in the considered phase p of cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; is the index number of the considered applicable WLTP test cycle; is the index of the individual phase within the applicable WLTP test cycle; is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven up to the end of the transition cycle n according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex; and: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.6.2.EQ-4] where: is the electric energy consumption of the considered phase p based on the REESS depletion of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, Wh/km; ECDC ,CD,p,c is the electric energy consumption of the considered phase p of cycle c based on the REESS depletion of the charge-depleting Type 1 test according to paragraph 4.3. of this annex, Wh/km; d_p,c is the distance driven in the considered phase p of cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; c is the index number of the considered applicable WLTP test cycle; p is the index of the individual phase within the applicable WLTP test cycle; n_c is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven up to the end of the transition cycle n according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex. The considered phase shall be the low phase, medium phase, high phase, extra high phase, and the city driving cycle.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.7">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4</data>
      <data key="d20">4.4.7</data>
      <data key="d27">4.4.7</data>
      <data key="d21">3</data>
      <data key="d22">497</data>
      <data key="d23">499</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Actual charge-depleting range for OVC-FCHVs</data>
      <data key="d24">The actual charge-depleting range shall be calculated using the following equation: For Level 1A and 4-phase WLTP test in Level 2 [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.7.EQ-1] For Level 1B and 3-phase WLTP test in Level 2 where: [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.7.EQ-2] is the actual charge-depleting range, km; is the charge-sustaining fuel consumption according to Table A8/7, step no. 5, kg/100km; is the charge-sustaining fuel efficiency according to Table A8/7, step no. 5, km/kg; is the fuel consumption of the applicable WLTP test cycle n of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, kg/100km; is the fuel efficiency of the applicable WLTP test cycle n of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km/kg; is the arithmetic average fuel consumption of the chargedepleting Type 1 test from the beginning up to and including the applicable WLTP test cycle (n-1), kg/100km; FECD,avg,n−1 is the arithmetic average fuel efficiency of the chargedepleting Type 1 test from the beginning up to and including the applicable WLTP test cycle (n-1), km/kg; d_c is the distance driven in the applicable WLTP test cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; d_n is the distance driven in the applicable WLTP test cycle n of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; c is the index number of the considered applicable WLTP test cycle; n is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven including the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex; and where [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.7.EQ-3] is the arithmetic average fuel consumption of the chargedepleting Type 1 test from the beginning up to and including the applicable WLTP test cycle (n-1), kg/100 km; FC_CD ,c is the fuel consumption of the applicable WLTP test cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, kg/100km; d_c is the distance driven in the applicable WLTP test cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; c is the index number of the considered applicable WLTP test cycle; n is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven including the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex. [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.7.EQ-4] is the arithmetic average fuel efficiency of the chargedepleting Type 1 test from the beginning up to and including the applicable WLTP test cycle (n-1), km/kg; FE_CD,c is the fuel efficiency of the applicable WLTP test cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km/kg; d_c is the distance driven in the applicable WLTP test cycle c of the charge-depleting Type 1 test, km; [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.4.7.EQ-5] is the index number of the considered applicable WLTP test cycle; is the number of applicable WLTP test cycles driven including the transition cycle according to paragraph 3.2.4.4. of this annex.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.4.5">
