      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">556</data>
      <data key="d23">556</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">Preconditioning</data>
      <data key="d24">The test vehicle shall be preconditioned according to paragraph 3.3.1.1. of this annex.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8.APP2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.APP2.3.2.2.2">
      <data key="d0">Clause</data>
      <data key="d1">REG154.04</data>
      <data key="d17">Clause</data>
      <data key="d18">decimal</data>
      <data key="d19">REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.APP2.3.2.2</data>
      <data key="d20">3.2.2.2</data>
      <data key="d27">3.2.2.2</data>
      <data key="d21">4</data>
      <data key="d22">556</data>
      <data key="d23">557</data>
      <data key="d28">True</data>
      <data key="d8">REESS adjustment</data>
      <data key="d24">After preconditioning, the soaking according to paragraph 3.3.1.2. of this annex shall be omitted and a break, during which the REESS is permitted to be adjusted, shall be set to a maximum duration of 60 minutes. A similar break shall be applied in advance of each test. Immediately after the end of this break, the requirements of paragraph 3.2.2.3. of this appendix shall be applied. Upon request of the manufacturer, an additional warm-up procedure may be conducted in advance of the REESS adjustment to ensure similar starting conditions for the correction coefficient determination. If the manufacturer [EQ:REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.APP2.3.2.2.2.EQ-1] requests this additional warm-up procedure, the identical warm-up procedure shall be applied repeatedly within the test sequence.</data>
      <data key="d25" />
      <data key="d26">True</data>
      <data key="d7">["Provision", "Paragraph"]</data>
      <data key="d29">ANNEX-B8.APP2</data>
    </node>
    <node id="REG154.04.ANNEX-B8.APP2.3.2.2.3">
